The build is complete and verified. All files exist on disk.
I built the Frontend Remix MVP per the design doc and plan, fixing the pre-existing corrupted/truncated assets and adding the missing style-picker logic.
What was done:
Core logic (verified on disk):
`content/style-engine.js` — Style registry with the 5-style `CATALOG`, `assetUrl()`, `injectCss()` (fetches bundled CSS and inlines it as `<style>` so host-page `style-src` CSP can't block it, with a `<link>` fallback), `applyIcons()`, `tagIcons()` (sets `data-frx-style` + `--frx-icon-*`), `applyStyle()` (returns a Promise), `clearStyle()`, `getCurrentStyle()`. Exposes `window.__frxStyleEngine`.

`content/content.js` — Existing font-swap logic (scan/apply/clear/reset, FontFace-from-bytes, `FRX_BG_FETCH_FONT`) left fully intact; `FRX_APPLY_STYLE`/`FRX_CLEAR_STYLE`/`FRX_GET_STYLE`/`FRX_PING` handlers delegate to the engine.

`background/background.js` — Message router; updated injection list to include `style-engine.js` so the engine is present when `FRX_BG_FORWARD` injects on demand. Font-download path unchanged.

`popup/popup.html` + `popup/popup.js` — Added the `#frx-style-picker` dropdown population from the `STYLES` catalog, change/clear handlers, status line, and `FRX_GET_STYLE` sync on load; guarded `showState` against missing loading/empty nodes. All existing font UI logic preserved.

`popup/popup.css` — Style-bar styling present.

`manifest.json` — MV3; `web_accessible_resources` broadened to `assets/*`, `assets/*/*`, `assets/*/*/*` so nested CSS/icons load over `chrome-extension://`.

Assets: All 5 style dirs (`brutalism`, `swiss`, `bento`, `editorial`, `retro-y2k`) each contain `fonts.css`, `borders.css`, `buttons.css`, `spacing.css`, `layout.css` and `icons/{arrow,check,close,settings}.svg`. `brutalism` had 3 truncated/corrupted files (`fonts.css`, `layout.css`) which I rewrote complete; all CSS passes brace-balance checks, all SVGs are well-formed, and all JS passes `node --check`.
Note: per the plan's "Out of scope", there is no GitHub push and no cross-tab style persistence (style state is per-page and lost on reload), as specified.
